<title>USA: Pension funds not following Philadelphia on Texaco.</title>
<headline>Pension funds not following Philadelphia on Texaco.</headline>
<byline>Jeffrey Benkoe</byline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-11-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Public pension funds that own stock in Texaco Inc have no plans to follow the lead of the city of Philadelphia's pension board and divest their shares in the oil giant.</p>
<p>The Philadelphia pension board voted on Thursday to divest $5.5 million worth of Texaco stock, citing evidence of racial bias at the oil company. The divestiture came after revelations that tape recordings of discussions among Texaco executives were laced with racial slurs.</p>
</text>
